        "mission_intent": "We need to assess and document our current log management infrastructure against NIST SP 800-92 guidance, specifically focusing on our second-tier architecture. Right now we have a single centralized log server handling collection, analysis, and both short-term and long-term storage for the entire enterprise, and leadership wants to understand the risks associated with this setup. Please evaluate whether our current single-server approach is appropriate given our organization's size and operational footprint, and produce a written gap analysis that addresses redundancy capabilities, failover arrangements for log generators if the primary server goes down, and whether we should move to a multi-server topology with specialized functions such as separating collection and analysis from long-term storage. The report should also cover whether our infrastructure supports log data sharing between servers for redundancy purposes. Include recommendations for any architectural changes needed and flag any scalability concerns. I'd like this delivered to the SOC leadership team by end of next week so we can incorporate findings into our quarterly infrastructure review.",
